# lib-sh-shims allow list — spira/lib.sh and spira/conf.sh real-bodied functions kept on
# purpose, with why. Shrinks as each is ported, retired, or its blocker clears; an entry
# naming a function that no longer exists is refused (lib_sh_shims.rs). One per line,
# `<file>:<function>`.
#
# Full audit: sp-hlng2 ("wave 4.37: close-out, lib.sh is shims only"), report in the bead.

# --- lib.sh: live bash callers outside the family the plan ported, or a suite that
# --- overrides a sibling function by name after sourcing this file (the EXEC-BOUNDARY
# --- TRAP: shimming onto a subprocess would make that override unreachable). Each is
# --- already named in this file's own header comment at the function's definition.
spira/lib.sh:host_cores
spira/lib.sh:ready_raw_args
spira/lib.sh:ready_count
spira/lib.sh:fayth_free

